---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Hello, there!</h1>
			<p>
				This was built off the official <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> blog starter template. 
				I reworked it to use it for displaying my obsidian vault. It didnt take too long at all.
				All I needed to change at first was the blogs folder to notes and to change notes/index.astro to work with my folders and notes.
			</p>
			<p>
				I have two helper functions, to get the file name and the folders that file belongs to. 
				I use github actions on live or a file path on local to get the data from my repo.
				I will probably write a blog on the process very soon so that other people can do this too.
			</p>
			<p>
				I wanted this to show my workings from University and projects, and to switch <a href="https://emmascott.dev/blog">my blog</a> from md files to my obsidian vault. 
				The obsidian vault is kept as a seperate repo, as on my main site every time I added a blog I'd have to make another patch version, 
				which I didn't like. This will replace that!
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
